<title>INDIA: India forex reserves rise to $22.75 bln on Sept 13.</title>
<headline>India forex reserves rise to $22.75 bln on Sept 13.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's foreign exchange reserves rose to $22.75 billion on September 13, 1996, from $22.68 billion the previous week, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said on Monday.</p>
<p>	 FOREIGN EXCHANGE RESERVES (in million U.S. dollars)</p>
<p>					  Sept 13     Sept 6	Sept 15</p>
<p>					    1996	  1996	   1995</p>
<p>    Foreign currency assets     18,143	18,044	 18,921</p>
<p>    Gold				 4,455	 4,455	  4,413</p>
<p>    SDRs				   155	   185	     47</p>
<p>    Total			     22,753	22,684	 23,381</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
